Let us start with Deutsch problem

# Deutsch problem

1. Problem statement:
We are given black-box access to a Boolean function

$$
f : \{0,1\} \to \{0,1\}.
$$

The task is to decide whether $f$ is **constant** or **balanced**.
**Constant** means that:
$$
f(0) = f(1).
$$
and **balanced** if
$$
f(0) \neq f(1).
$$

2. Challenges:
There are exactly four possible such functions:
$$
\begin{array}{c|cc|c}
& f(0) & f(1) & \text{type} \\
\hline
f_1 & 0 & 0 & \text{constant} \\
f_2 & 1 & 1 & \text{constant} \\
f_3 & 0 & 1 & \text{balanced} \\
f_4 & 1 & 0 & \text{balanced}
\end{array}
$$

If we want to solve the problem, we need to evaluate both values
$$
f(0)
\qquad \text{and} \qquad
f(1).
$$
So a classical deterministic algorithm needs two oracle queries.

3. Quantum approach:
The quantum algorithm solves the problem with one oracle query.


